{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790262882837,"sessionID":"ses_f2c04ba18ffe2VBe3QmPqD6n7p","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02128589fac14d3e8168dd06","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/project.godot"},"output":"<path>/workspace/project.godot</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ; Engine configuration file.\n2: ; It's best edited using the editor UI and not directly,\n3: ; since the parameters that go here are not all obvious.\n4: ;\n5: ; Format:\n6: ;   [section] ; section goes between []\n7: ;   param=value ; assign values to parameters\n8: \n9: config_version=5\n10: \n11: [application]\n12: \n13: config/name=\"Outline Compute Shader\"\n14: config/description=\"Implement a compositor compute shader and GDScript pipeline for a depth outline effect.\"\n15: run/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\n16: config/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.5\", \"Forward Plus\")\n17: \n18: [rendering]\n19: \n20: renderer/rendering_method=\"forward_plus\"\n\n(End of file - total 20 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"; Engine configuration file.\n; It's best edited using the editor UI and not directly,\n; since the parameters that go here are not all obvious.\n;\n; Format:\n;   [section] ; section goes between []\n;   param=value ; assign values to parameters\n\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\n\nconfig/name=\"Outline Compute Shader\"\nconfig/description=\"Implement a compositor compute shader and GDScript pipeline for a depth outline effect.\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.5\", \"Forward Plus\")\n\n[rendering]\n\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"forward_plus\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/project.godot","text":"; Engine configuration file.\n; It's best edited using the editor UI and not directly,\n; since the parameters that go here are not all obvious.\n;\n; Format:\n;   [section] ; section goes between []\n;   param=value ; assign values to parameters\n\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\n\nconfig/name=\"Outline Compute Shader\"\nconfig/description=\"Implement a compositor compute shader and GDScript pipeline for a depth outline effect.\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.5\", \"Forward Plus\")\n\n[rendering]\n\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"forward_plus\"","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":20,"totalLines":20,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/project.godot","time":{"start":1790262882803,"end":1790262882834}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_67e3de3e-1f1f-47d6-8285-aac5fe1df7fa"}},"id":"prt_0d3fbb1ec001hCHeN9qz1z350M","sessionID":"ses_f2c04ba18ffe2VBe3QmPqD6n7p","messageID":"msg_0d3fb8183001q3P0YLqiIaKx0j"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790262882837,"sessionID":"ses_f2c04ba18ffe2VBe3QmPqD6n7p","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_b0a9127d7255498e96455353","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/task_config.json"},"output":"<path>/workspace/task_config.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"instruction\": \"Implement `res://scripts/outline_effect.gd` and `res://outline.glsl` for a depth-based outline compositor effect. The script must include `@tool`, `extends CompositorEffect`, and `class_name OutlineEffect`. It must use `RenderingServer.get_rendering_device()` and create the compute pipeline with `rd.compute_pipeline_create`, a parameter storage buffer with `storage_buffer_create`, and a depth sampler with `sampler_create`. In the render callback, it must call `get_render_scene_buffers`, `get_internal_size`, `get_color_layer(0)`, and `get_depth_layer(0)`, update the buffer with `buffer_update`, create the uniform set with `uniform_set_create`, and dispatch with `compute_list_dispatch`. The shader must be a compute shader (`#[compute]`) with `layout(local_size_x = 8` and declare the params buffer as `readonly buffer Params` that includes `mat4 inv_proj_mat`. It must bind the color image as `uniform image2D color_image` and the depth texture as `sampler2D depth_texture` (with `binding = 0` on the params buffer). The shader must use `gl_GlobalInvocationID`, call a `get_linear_depth` function, use a `sample_size` radius to compare neighboring depths, and write the outlined color back with `imageStore`.\"\n3: }\n\n(End of file - total 3 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"instruction\": \"Implement `res://scripts/outline_effect.gd` and `res://outline.glsl` for a depth-based outline compositor effect. The script must include `@tool`, `extends CompositorEffect`, and `class_name OutlineEffect`. It must use `RenderingServer.get_rendering_device()` and create the compute pipeline with `rd.compute_pipeline_create`, a parameter storage buffer with `storage_buffer_create`, and a depth sampler with `sampler_create`. In the render callback, it must call `get_render_scene_buffers`, `get_internal_size`, `get_color_layer(0)`, and `get_depth_layer(0)`, update the buffer with `buffer_update`, create the uniform set with `uniform_set_create`, and dispatch with `compute_list_dispatch`. The shader must be a compute shader (`#[compute]`) with `layout(local_size_x = 8` and declare the params buffer as `readonly buffer Params` that includes `mat4 inv_proj_mat`. It must bind the color image as `uniform image2D color_image` and the depth texture as `sampler2D depth_texture` (with `binding = 0` on the params buffer). The shader must use `gl_GlobalInvocationID`, call a `get_linear_depth` function, use a `sample_size` radius to compare neighboring depths, and write the outlined color back with `imageStore`.\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/task_config.json","text":"{\n  \"instruction\": \"Implement `res://scripts/outline_effect.gd` and `res://outline.glsl` for a depth-based outline compositor effect. The script must include `@tool`, `extends CompositorEffect`, and `class_name OutlineEffect`. It must use `RenderingServer.get_rendering_device()` and create the compute pipeline with `rd.compute_pipeline_create`, a parameter storage buffer with `storage_buffer_create`, and a depth sampler with `sampler_create`. In the render callback, it must call `get_render_scene_buffers`, `get_internal_size`, `get_color_layer(0)`, and `get_depth_layer(0)`, update the buffer with `buffer_update`, create the uniform set with `uniform_set_create`, and dispatch with `compute_list_dispatch`. The shader must be a compute shader (`#[compute]`) with `layout(local_size_x = 8` and declare the params buffer as `readonly buffer Params` that includes `mat4 inv_proj_mat`. It must bind the color image as `uniform image2D color_image` and the depth texture as `sampler2D depth_texture` (with `binding = 0` on the params buffer). The shader must use `gl_GlobalInvocationID`, call a `get_linear_depth` function, use a `sample_size` radius to compare neighboring depths, and write the outlined color back with `imageStore`.\"\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":3,"totalLines":3,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/task_config.json","time":{"start":1790262882813,"end":1790262882836}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_ba1676df-694b-4411-be13-bbf43ddb398b"}},"id":"prt_0d3fbb1f7001ussutgoiv7MKMd","sessionID":"ses_f2c04ba18ffe2VBe3QmPqD6n7p","messageID":"msg_0d3fb8183001q3P0YLqiIaKx0j"}}
